 F(1, RESHAPE, "This code should print the 6 numbers as 3 rows of 2, but it crashes. Fix the reshape.", NP + 'a = np.arange(1, 7)\nprint(a.reshape(4, 2))', NP + 'a = np.arange(1, 7)\nprint(a.reshape(3, 2))', "A reshape must keep the number of values: 6 values fit 3 x 2, not 4 x 2 (which needs 8)."),
 # ---------- Medium ----------
 W(2, RESHAPE, '`daily = np.arange(1, 15)` (14 days). Reshape it into 2 weeks x 7 days and print the result.', NP + 'daily = np.arange(1, 15)\n', NP + 'daily = np.arange(1, 15)\nprint(daily.reshape(2, 7))', "14 values fit exactly into 2 rows of 7. Each row is one week."),
 W(2, COMBINE, '`q1 = np.array([100, 120])` and `q2 = np.array([130, 150])`. Print them joined into one row, then stacked as two rows.', NP + 'q1 = np.array([100, 120])\nq2 = np.array([130, 150])\n', NP + 'q1 = np.array([100, 120])\nq2 = np.array([130, 150])\nprint(np.concatenate([q1, q2]))\nprint(np.vstack([q1, q2]))', "`concatenate` puts arrays end to end. `vstack` puts them on top of each other as rows."),
 T(2, DTYPE, NP + 'print(np.array([3.7, -1.2, 9.9]).astype(int))', "`astype(int)` cuts off the decimal part (towards 0). It does not round, so 3.7 becomes 3 and -1.2 becomes -1."),
 W(2, DIMS, 'Make a 3D array with `np.arange(12).reshape(2, 2, 3)`. Print its number of dimensions, then the value at position `[1, 0, 2]`.', NP, NP + 'cube = np.arange(12).reshape(2, 2, 3)\nprint(cube.ndim)\nprint(cube[1, 0, 2])', "A 3D array has blocks, rows and columns. Block 1, row 0, column 2 holds the value 8."),
 W(2, CREATE, 'Print a 3 x 3 identity matrix with `np.eye`, then a 2 x 2 array where every value is 7, with `np.full`.', NP, NP + 'print(np.eye(3))\nprint(np.full((2, 2), 7))', "`eye` puts 1s on the diagonal (as floats). `full` fills every place with the value you give."),
 F(2, DTYPE, "This code should print the total `600`, but it fails. Fix the array.", NP + 'prices = np.array([100, "200", 300])\nprint(prices.sum())', NP + 'prices = np.array([100, 200, 300])\nprint(prices.sum())', "One text value turns the whole array into text, and text cannot be added up. Keep the numbers as numbers."),
 T(2, PROPS, NP + 'm = np.ones((3, 4))\nprint(m.shape, m.size, m.ndim, len(m))', "3 rows of 4 values: 12 in total, 2 dimensions. `len()` of a 2D array counts its rows."),
 W(2, RESHAPE, '`grid = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]])`. Print it flattened into one row, then reshaped into 2 rows and 3 columns.', NP + 'grid = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]])\n', NP + 'grid = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]])\nprint(grid.flatten())\nprint(grid.reshape(2, 3))', "`flatten()` gives a 1D copy. `reshape(2, 3)` fills the new shape row by row with the same 6 values."),
